---
title: Dinner rolls
servings: 16
yield: 16 rolls
tags: [american, vegetarian, thanksgiving, holiday]
cuisine: american
time: 2 hours 45 minutes
source: Soft Dinner Rolls by King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/soft-dinner-rolls-recipe
---

Mix the @instant yeast{7%g}, @granulated sugar{39%g}, @table salt{8%g}, @all-purpose flour{360%g}, @potato flakes{46%g}(or 46 g potato flour), @water{71%g}(lukewarm; potato water if you have it), @milk{170%g}(lukewarm) and @unsalted butter{43%g}(softened or melted) into a soft dough.

Knead ~{6%minutes} in a #stand mixer{} on low, or ~{8%minutes} by hand, until smooth and springy.

Cover in a greased bowl and let rise ~{1%hour} to 2 hours, until doubled.

Turn it out, press out the air and cut it into 16 pieces of about 45 g. Roll each into a tight ball.

Set them in a greased #9-by-13-inch metal pan{} (or two 9-inch round pans). Cover and let rise ~{1%hour}, until puffy and touching. Heat the oven to 350°F near the end.

Bake ~{20%minutes} to 22 minutes, until golden. Brush the tops with melted butter while warm if you like, and cool on a rack.
